# Security and quality

- Keep `DATABASE_URL`, session tokens, passwords, and private upload paths server-only. Never add them to client-side code, logs, examples, or commits.
- Treat route input, uploaded filenames, MIME types, and IDs as untrusted. Validate them before using them in queries or filesystem operations.
- Keep Drizzle schema changes and generated migrations in source control. Do not commit local database data or contents of `uploads/`.
- Prefer updating the existing helpers, components, and route handlers over introducing duplicate abstractions or a second backend.
- Preserve established API response shapes unless the associated client code is updated in the same change.
- After application code changes, run `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` when practical.
